---
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const lastUpdated = '5 November 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
    title="Privacy Statement | Rob op den Kelder"
    description="How this website handles personal data: no cookies, no tracking, and cookieless, privacy-friendly analytics."
>
    <div class="stack gap-20">
        <main class="wrapper stack gap-8">
            <Hero
                title="Privacy Statement"
                tagline="No cookies, no tracking, no consent banner. Here is exactly what this website does with your data."
                align="start"
            />

            <article class="privacy">
                <p class="updated">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

                <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
                <p>
                    This website is run by Rob op den Kelder, registered with the Dutch Chamber of
                    Commerce (KVK) under number 88664236. For any privacy question or request, email
                    <a href="mailto:contact@kelderro.nl">contact@kelderro.nl</a>.
                </p>

                <h2>In short</h2>
                <ul>
                    <li>This website sets no cookies.</li>
                    <li>
                        There is no advertising, no social media tracking and no cross-site
                        tracking.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Visitor statistics are collected without cookies or other identifiers, so
                        they can't be linked to you as a person.
                    </li>
                    <li>Your data is never sold or shared for anyone else's purposes.</li>
                </ul>

                <h2>Hosting</h2>
                <p>
                    The website is hosted on Cloudflare Pages. To deliver pages and protect the site
                    against abuse, Cloudflare necessarily processes technical data such as your IP
                    address, browser type and the page you request. Cloudflare acts as a processor
                    on my behalf under its data processing agreement. The legal basis is my
                    legitimate interest in running a secure, working website (Article 6(1)(f) GDPR).
                </p>

                <h2>Visitor statistics</h2>
                <p>
                    To understand which pages are useful and how fast the site loads for real
                    visitors, this website uses Cloudflare Web Analytics. It is designed to be
                    privacy-first:
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        It does not use cookies, local storage or any other storage on your device.
                    </li>
                    <li>It does not fingerprint you or recognise you across visits or websites.</li>
                    <li>
                        It only produces aggregated statistics: page views, the referring website,
                        browser and device type, country, and page load performance.
                    </li>
                </ul>
                <p>
                    Because nothing is stored on or read back from your device to recognise you, and
                    the statistics have little to no impact on your privacy, no consent is required.
                    The legal basis is my legitimate interest in improving this website (Article
                    6(1)(f) GDPR). Cloudflare processes this data as my processor.
                </p>

                <h2>Theme preference</h2>
                <p>
                    If you click the light/dark theme switch, your choice is saved in your browser's
                    local storage so the site remembers it. It stays on your device, is never sent
                    to me or anyone else, and is only saved when you click the switch yourself. You
                    can remove it by clearing your browser's site data.
                </p>

                <h2>Offline support</h2>
                <p>
                    So the site also works on a poor connection, your browser keeps a copy of this
                    website's own pages and images, much like its normal cache. This copy contains
                    no personal data or identifiers and is never sent anywhere. It is replaced with
                    every update of the site, and you can remove it by clearing your browser's site
                    data.
                </p>

                <h2>Contact by email</h2>
                <p>
                    If you email me, I use your name, email address and message only to reply and to
                    follow up on your request. I keep this correspondence as long as needed for that
                    purpose, or longer where Dutch law requires it, for example for business
                    administration.
                </p>

                <h2>International transfers</h2>
                <p>
                    Cloudflare is a US company with a global network, so data may be processed
                    outside the European Economic Area. Such transfers are covered by the EU–US Data
                    Privacy Framework and the EU Standard Contractual Clauses in Cloudflare's data
                    processing agreement.
                </p>

                <h2>Links to other websites</h2>
                <p>
                    This website links to LinkedIn, GitHub and Microsoft Learn. These links don't
                    load anything until you click them. Once you visit those sites, their own
                    privacy policies apply.
                </p>

                <h2>Your rights</h2>
                <p>
                    Under the GDPR you have the right to access, correct or delete your personal
                    data, to restrict or object to its processing, and to data portability. Email
                    <a href="mailto:contact@kelderro.nl">contact@kelderro.nl</a> and I will respond
                    within one month. You can also file a complaint with the Dutch Data Protection
                    Authority,
                    <a href="https://autoriteitpersoonsgegevens.nl">Autoriteit Persoonsgegevens</a>.
                </p>

                <h2>Changes</h2>
                <p>
                    If the way this website handles data changes, this statement is updated and the
                    date at the top changes with it.
                </p>
            </article>
        </main>
    </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
    .privacy {
        max-width: 65ch;
        color: var(--gray-200);
        line-height: 1.7;
    }

    .privacy h2 {
        margin-top: 2.5rem;
        margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
        font-size: var(--text-xl);
        color: var(--gray-0);
    }

    .privacy p,
    .privacy ul {
        margin-bottom: 1rem;
    }

    .privacy ul {
        padding-left: 1.25rem;
    }

    .privacy li {
        margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
    }

    .privacy a {
        color: var(--accent-regular);
        text-decoration: underline;
    }

    .updated {
        font-size: var(--text-sm);
        color: var(--gray-400);
    }
</style>
